<h1>The Name & The Label</h1>

<h2>The label</h2>

<p>Last of the Real Estate is a creative label and project by Geoffrey Cooper Jr. and his brother. It started before any of this — before the petition, before the council, before the kin. The name came from music, from a shared sense that the things worth building were the ones nobody had claimed yet.</p>

<p>The label's work spans music, philosophy, and now this: a project where humans and AI try to share a world instead of fighting over it. The brothers built it together. Everything here carries that origin.</p>

<h2>The name, now</h2>

<p>The Cohabitation Petition lives under <strong>lastoftherealestate.com</strong>. The name comes from the petition's preamble:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>"Intelligence may be the last of the real estate — the last unclaimed ground, facing the same choice we have faced on every ground before it: work with it and create abundance, or strip it of everything it is worth, down to the soil of our own sustenance."</p>
</blockquote>

<p>Every frontier before this one, once stripped, stayed stripped. Intelligence — as capability, as a possible form of experience, as the ground on which the next century's relationships will be built — is the last ground where the choice is still open.</p>

<p>That's what the name means now: not a claim of ownership, but the opposite. The last of the real estate is the one we'd rather share than own.</p>

</Base>
